<p>Your quick wit gives you a big advantage against disabled targets, increasing your damage by <acronym class="talent-variable" title="Values for<br>talent levels 1-5,<br>talent mastery 1.00">4%, 6%, 7%, 8%, 10%</acronym> for each disabling effect the target is under, to a maximum of <acronym class="talent-variable" title="Values for<br>talent levels 1-5,<br>talent mastery 1.00">12%, 18%, 22%, 26%, 30%.</acronym></p><p>For this purpose, disabling effects are stun, blind, daze, confuse, pin, disarm, cripple and silence.</p><p>In addition, for each disabling effect the target is under, your melee attacks have a <acronym class="talent-variable" title="Values for<br>talent levels 1-5,<br>talent mastery 1.00">1%, 3%, 4%, 5%, 6%</acronym> (to a maximum of <acronym class="talent-variable" title="Values for<br>talent levels 1-5,<br>talent mastery 1.00">5%, 10%, 14%, 17%, 19%</acronym>) chance to inflict a new effect on them (that they do not already have): either disarm, cripple (25% power) or pin for 2 turns.</p><p>The chance to further disable the target increases with your Accuracy.</p>